reply:
The crash comes from a getter that calls itself. In `cart.mjs:15`, `get total()` returns `this.total`, and reading `this.total` runs the same getter again. That repeats until the stack overflows, giving `RangeError: Maximum call stack size exceeded`. The first checkout hit it at `app.mjs:8` (`formatPence(cart.total)`).

The class stores the running sum in `this._total` (set in the constructor at line 6, updated in `add()` at line 11). The getter should return that field instead:

```js
  get total() {
    return this._total;
  }
```

This is the only caller I found. `app.mjs:8` only reads `cart.total`, and nothing assigns to it, so you don't need a setter. I didn't run anything because you're making the change yourself.

To check it, run one checkout request after the fix and confirm the response has a `total`. There's no cart test yet. `money.test.mjs` covers `money.mjs` only.

