The fix is one line. Return the backin' field that `add()` already keeps up to date:

```js
get total() {
  return this._total;
}
```

`_total` starts at `0` in the constructor and `add()` does `this._total += price * qty`. Nuffin' else reads or writes `total` (I grepped `app.mjs`, `money.mjs`, `money.test.mjs`), so swappin' the name won't break any callers.

